# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MuAPI media provider — configuration template
#
# COPY THESE LINES INTO apps/web/.env.local (or the Vercel project settings).
# DO NOT fill the key values in this file: `.gitignore` blanket-ignores `.env*`,
# which is why this template is named `*.env.example` instead — it is TRACKED,
# so anything written here is committed. The two key lines below must stay empty.
#
# The shipped defaults are the harmless ones: MuAPI disabled, mode test.
# `lib/qa/muapi-media-provider.test.ts` fails if that ever stops being true.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Master switch. Accepts `1` or `true`; anything else (including absent) is off.
# Off means NO outbound MuAPI call of any kind — not generation, not polling,
# not a health check.
MUAPI_ENABLED=false

# `test` or `production`. Anything unrecognised resolves to `test`.
# Setting this to `production` does nothing on its own — see below.
MUAPI_MODE=test

# Sandbox credential. Create it at https://muapi.ai/access-keys with
# `is_test: true`; such keys return mock outputs and are NEVER billed.
MUAPI_TEST_API_KEY=

# Live credential. Billed on completion. Only ever read when MUAPI_MODE=production
# AND MUAPI_PRODUCTION_ENABLED=1. Its mere presence never selects production.
MUAPI_PROD_API_KEY=

# The second switch production requires. Two switches, because one switch is one
# typo. Leave this unset until a spend policy and an approval gate exist.
# MUAPI_PRODUCTION_ENABLED=1

# Optional base URL override. Defaults to https://api.muapi.ai
# MUAPI_BASE_URL=
